    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0648" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/7577: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-01-13T19:00:00+02:00">January 13, 1941—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 13—2:52 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Embassy has received a report that during an audience which the Secretary of
                    the Fascist Party in Albania had with the Duce<anchor n="6" xml:id="d598-f1"/>
                    on January 9, the former tendered his resignation. The Duce insisted, however,
                    that the Secretary retain his post adding that the present situation in Albania
                    would soon undergo a change for the better as the Germans had promised to extend
                    military aid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d598-f1" n="6" xml:id="d598-f1-content">
                <p>Benito Mussolini, Italian Prime Minister.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
